          "title": "Evaluate fraction",
          "body": "\\[\nf(x)=2x-3,\\qquad g(x)=\\frac{x}{3x+1}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "(a) The denominator of cannot",
          "body": "(a) The denominator of \\(g\\) cannot be zero:\n\\[\n3x+1=0\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx=-\\frac13\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "(b)",
          "body": "(b)\n\\[\ngf(x)=g(f(x))\n\\]\n\n\\[\ngf(x)=\\frac{2x-3}{3(2x-3)+1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\ngf(x)=\\frac{2x-3}{6x-8}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "(c) Let",
          "body": "(c) Let\n\\[\ny=\\frac{x}{3x+1}\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny(3x+1)=x\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3xy+y=x\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx(3y-1)=-y\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx=\\frac{y}{1-3y}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Evaluate fraction",
          "body": "So\n\\[\ng^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x}{1-3x}\n\\]"
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "Excluded value \\(-\\frac13\\), \\(gf(x)=\\dfrac{2x-3}{6x-8}\\), and \\(g^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{x}{1-3x}\\)."
    },
