          "title": "Use trigonometry",
          "body": "The sphere has diameter \\(x\\), so its radius is\n\n\\[\n\\frac x2\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "The volume of the sphere",
          "body": "The volume of the sphere is \\(288\\pi\\text{ cm}^3\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac43\\pi\\left(\\frac x2\\right)^3=288\\pi\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi x^3}{6}=288\\pi\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx^3=1728\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx=12\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "The rectangular base of the",
          "body": "The rectangular base of the pyramid has dimensions \\(x\\) and \\(2x\\), so its area is\n\n\\[\nx(2x)=2x^2\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use trigonometry",
          "body": "For the two faces with base \\(x\\), the slant height is\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(5x)^2+x^2}=x\\sqrt{26}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Their total area is",
          "body": "Their total area is\n\n\\[\n2\\left(\\frac12 x\\cdot x\\sqrt{26}\\right)=x^2\\sqrt{26}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use trigonometry",
          "body": "For the two faces with base \\(2x\\), the slant height is\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(5x)^2+\\left(\\frac x2\\right)^2}\n=\\frac{x\\sqrt{101}}2\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Their total area is",
          "body": "Their total area is\n\n\\[\n2\\left(\\frac12(2x)\\cdot\\frac{x\\sqrt{101}}2\\right)=x^2\\sqrt{101}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Total surface area",
          "body": "Total surface area:\n\n\\[\n2x^2+x^2\\sqrt{26}+x^2\\sqrt{101}\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Substitute",
          "body": "Substitute \\(x=12\\):\n\n\\[\n144(2+\\sqrt{26}+\\sqrt{101})=2469.440\\ldots\n\\]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Correct to the nearest",
          "body": "Correct to the nearest \\(\\text{cm}^2\\):\n\n\\[\n2469\n\\]"
